From: Redmi AX3000 NSS integration
Subject: [PATCH] qdisc: report lost statistics replies outside system load

The stats worker waits for an asynchronous firmware response, not disk I/O.
TASK_UNINTERRUPTIBLE counts that recurring wait toward load average even when
there is no CPU work or blocked storage. Use TASK_IDLE for this bounded,
stop-aware wait, retaining its wakeup and timeout semantics.

On STA-r50 most roots refresh only every 10-30 s because many SYNC_MANY
requests receive no reply within the 10 s command timeout. Upstream logged
each timeout; keep that report, rate limited, so the lost replies remain
visible once the wait no longer inflates the load average.

--- a/nss_qdisc/nss_qdisc_stats.c
+++ b/nss_qdisc/nss_qdisc_stats.c
@@ -554,7 +554,7 @@ static void nss_qdisc_stats_sync_msg_tx(struct nss_qdisc_stats_wq *nqsw)
 			continue;
 		}
 		nqsw->stats_request_success++;
-		wait_event_timeout(nqsw->stats_resp_waitqueue,
+		wait_event_idle_timeout(nqsw->stats_resp_waitqueue,
 			READ_ONCE(nqsw->stats_polling_stopped) ||
 			!atomic_read(&nqsw->pending_stat_resp), NSS_QDISC_COMMAND_TIMEOUT);
 		spin_lock_bh(&nss_qdisc_stats_list_lock);
@@ -569,6 +569,8 @@ static void nss_qdisc_stats_sync_msg_tx(struct nss_qdisc_stats_wq *nqsw)
 			return;
 		atomic_set(&nqsw->pending_stat_resp, 0);
 		nqsw->stats_request_fail++;
+		pr_warn_ratelimited("nss_qdisc: stats root %x got no reply (attempt %d, failures %lu)\n",
+				    nq->qos_tag, retry + 1, nqsw->stats_request_fail);
 	}
 	if (!READ_ONCE(nqsw->stats_polling_stopped)) {
 		stats->count = 0;
